2:Td26,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Article","headline":"IPTV vs Netflix in the UK: Which One Fits How You Watch?","description":"IPTV vs Netflix for UK viewers: live channels, Premier League coverage, catch-up, setup, and the real 2026 cost of running one service or both. An honest comparison.","image":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/images/guides/iptv-vs-netflix.svg","dateModified":"2026-08-04","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/iptv-vs-netflix-uk","url":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/iptv-vs-netflix-uk","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"IPTV UK","url":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/icon.svg"}},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"IPTV UK","url":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/icon.svg"}}},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Does IPTV replace Netflix?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not completely. IPTV may cover scheduled channels, catch-up programmes and a separate on-demand library, but Netflix Originals remain tied to Netflix. Check your recent viewing history before cancelling."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I watch the Premier League on Netflix?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Netflix carries selected live events, but it does not hold UK Premier League rights. Official coverage is available through licensed sports broadcasters. Saturday 3pm matches remain inside the UK broadcast blackout, so claims of authorised access to every fixture should be checked carefully."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is IPTV cheaper than Netflix?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can be, but always check how the monthly figure is calculated. Our 12-month Ultimate Plan is £49.99 paid upfront, which works out at roughly £4.17 a month, while the 1-month Starter Plan is £14.99. Netflix starts at £5.99 per month and allows monthly cancellation, so a short IPTV plan and a Netflix subscription can cost about the same."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need a TV Licence for IPTV or Netflix?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You need a UK TV Licence when you watch programmes or events live through IPTV, Netflix or another streaming platform. A licence is also required whenever you use BBC iPlayer, including on-demand programmes. You do not need one when you only watch standard on-demand Netflix films and series and never use BBC iPlayer. The same rules apply on televisions, phones, tablets and laptops."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use Netflix and IPTV on the same television?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Usually, yes. Netflix and an IPTV player can run on the same compatible Smart TV or streaming device. App availability varies between television operating systems, so check whether your device supports the required IPTV player before subscribing. A Fire TV Stick or another streaming device may be needed when the television’s app store does not carry it."}}]},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Guides","item":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/guides"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"IPTV vs Netflix UK","item":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/iptv-vs-netflix-uk"}]}]}6:["guideSlug","iptv-vs-netflix-uk","d"]
